==============================================================================
  Mutation tests  (assertion-strength validation)
==============================================================================

  Strategy: replace each named fact's body with `{}` (no constraint),
  then re-run Alloy. Each listed assertion should now FAIL on the
  mutated model. If it still PASSes, the assertion is vacuous and
  must be strengthened.

  - MUTATE F_LeastPrivilege  → runs/A-L1/mutated_F_LeastPrivilege.als
    rationale: Without F_LeastPrivilege, nothing forces successful operations to lie inside the permission matrix. Injecting a successful Customer GetAudit op contradicts (CustomerRole -> GetAudit not in Allowed), so the LeastPrivilege assertion must surface a counterexample.
    expected to FAIL: LeastPrivilege, FR_015_CustomersCantDecideOrAudit
      - LeastPrivilege: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_015_CustomersCantDecideOrAudit: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_OnePendingPerCustomer  → runs/A-L1/mutated_F_OnePendingPerCustomer.als
    rationale: Removing the partial-unique-index analogue lets the model invent two PendingReview applications for the same customer, which is exactly FR-005's prohibition.
    expected to FAIL: FR_005_OnePendingPerCustomer
      - FR_005_OnePendingPerCustomer: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_AppendOnlyAuditEntries  → runs/A-L1/mutated_F_AppendOnlyAuditEntries.als
    rationale: Clearing this fact removes the (app, eventType) uniqueness on the audit log; injecting two distinct events for the same application and type produces a structural violation the AppendOnly assertion must catch.
    expected to FAIL: AppendOnly
      - AppendOnly: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_AuditCompleteness  → runs/A-L1/mutated_F_AuditCompleteness.als
    rationale: Without F_AuditCompleteness no fact mandates a decision event per decided application. Injecting an Approved application with zero matching approved events flunks the AuditCompleteness assertion.
    expected to FAIL: AuditCompleteness, FR_014_NotificationOnDecision, FR_016_AuditTrail
      - AuditCompleteness: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_014_NotificationOnDecision: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_016_AuditTrail: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_OneDecisionPerApplication  → runs/A-L1/mutated_F_OneDecisionPerApplication.als
    rationale: The PK on decisions.application_id is what guarantees SC-005. Drop the fact and inject two Decision atoms pointing at the same LoanApplication; ConcurrencySafety must report a counterexample.
    expected to FAIL: ConcurrencySafety, FR_011_NoSecondDecision, FR_012_ConcurrentDecisionSafe
      - ConcurrencySafety: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_011_NoSecondDecision: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_012_ConcurrentDecisionSafe: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_OwnershipForGet  → runs/A-L1/mutated_F_OwnershipForGet.als
    rationale: Without ownership-gated access, the model can let a customer successfully GET another customer's application. The injection forces such a witness and the ownership-based-access predicates fail.
    expected to FAIL: OwnershipBasedAccess, NoInformationLeakage, FR_013_CustomerSeesOwnOnly
      - OwnershipBasedAccess: FAIL (expected)
      - NoInformationLeakage: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_013_CustomerSeesOwnOnly: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_AuditAttribution  → runs/A-L1/mutated_F_AuditAttribution.als
    rationale: F_AuditAttribution is the only constraint that binds an approved/rejected event's actor to staff. Removing it and injecting an Approved event whose actor is a Customer produces a clear AttributionCorrectness counterexample.
    expected to FAIL: AttributionCorrectness
      - AttributionCorrectness: FAIL (expected)

